+# Narrowing the Veterinarian Directory by Specialty
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+NG-9 declined search for a pet, a visit, or a veterinarian, leaving owners the only searchable entity. The row was derived from observed absence during the 2026-07-31 bootstrap survey, so whether it was a decision or an accident stayed unknown.
+
+A request to narrow the veterinarian directory to one specialty reached the boundary on 2026-09-06. Read broadly, NG-9 declines it. Read narrowly, NG-9 declines free-text search, and narrowing a published list by an attribute it already shows is a different capability.
+
+The same request touches a second recorded boundary. `REQ-VET-002` — the machine-readable veterinarian list — was withdrawn on 2026-07-31 as an implementation artifact with no consumer.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Hold NG-9 whole.** Decline the request. Rejected by the owner: the row's rationale is about repeating owner search, which this capability does not do.
+2. **Retire NG-9.** Open search across pets, visits, and veterinarians. Rejected: the rationale still holds for free-text search, and the breadth teaches nothing new.
+3. **Narrow NG-9** (chosen). Free-text search stays out; narrowing the directory by a specialty it already lists comes in.
+
+## Decision
+
+NG-9 is narrowed, not retired. Free-text search for a pet, a visit, or a veterinarian remains out of scope. Narrowing the veterinarian directory to the veterinarians holding one named specialty is in scope, on both published surfaces.
+
+The machine-readable surface is reinstated as supported and carries the capability. `REQ-VET-002` stays withdrawn and its id is not reused; `REQ-VET-003` states the reinstated surface and the narrowing as a fresh requirement.
+
+The narrowing is exercised by naming the specialty in the request. Neither surface gains a form, a dropdown, or any other page control in this round. A visible control is a separate request the owner may raise later.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- NG-9 leaves the open provenance consultation as a decided row. Its remaining scope is free-text search alone.
+- A second capability now depends on the machine-readable surface, so removing that surface is no longer a maintenance option.
+- The directory gains a capability with no visible affordance. A reader who does not know the capability exists cannot discover it from the page.
+- A later request for a visible control, or for combining several specialties, is new scope and re-enters at intake.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-9
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the narrowed row and the preamble naming it decided.
+- [PRD REQ-VET-003](../prd.md#req-vet-003) — the requirement the narrowing admits.
