+# Specialty-Filtered Veterinarian Reads Are Not Cached
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+Both read methods on `VetRepository` are annotated `@Cacheable("vets")`. `CacheConfiguration` creates that cache with statistics enabled and nothing else — no expiry policy and no size limit. Its own source comment records that a size limit must come from the chosen provider. The application has no write path for veterinarians, so nothing evicts an entry either.
+
+`REQ-VET-003` adds an optional specialty parameter to both published veterinarian surfaces. The narrowing runs as a repository query, so the specialty name joins the cache key wherever that query is cached. The value is caller-supplied, and every route is open to every caller — see [system-design.md § Security Context](../system-design.md#security-context).
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Cache the filtered reads like the unfiltered ones.** Consistent with the neighbouring methods. Rejected: an anonymous caller would then choose keys in a cache that never evicts, so distinct values accumulate without bound.
+2. **Cache them behind a bounded, expiring cache.** Requires selecting a JCache provider policy for the whole application. Rejected here: that resets the caching baseline for every cached read, and [open question 5](../system-design.md#open-questions-from-the-survey) on vet cache invalidation is unsettled.
+3. **Leave the filtered reads uncached** (chosen). The unfiltered reads keep their caching; a narrowed request reaches the database.
+
+## Decision
+
+The specialty-filtered veterinarian queries carry no `@Cacheable` annotation. The two unfiltered reads keep theirs unchanged.
+
+A request-derived value does not become a key in the `vets` cache while that cache has neither an eviction policy nor a size limit.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- A narrowed request costs one database round trip. The clinic's directory is small, so the cost is slight.
+- Two neighbouring repository methods now differ in caching. A reader who notices the asymmetry is answered here.
+- Configuring a bounded provider policy would remove the constraint. The decision is revisited when open question 5 is settled.
+- The rule generalizes: any later query keyed by caller input faces the same bar while the cache stays unbounded.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Requirements:** REQ-VET-003
+
+## References
+
+- [system-design.md § Contracts](../system-design.md#contracts) — the veterinarian repository row carrying this rule.
+- [Narrowing the Veterinarian Directory by Specialty](2026-09-06-non-goal-veterinarian-search.md) — the product decision this serves.
